ublican groups follow through on promised spending for Merrin, and any late polling movement on cost-of-living issues, could shift this toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Marcy Kaptur (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Marcy Kaptur, one of the longest-serving House members, seeks another term in a northern Ohio district drawn to lean Republican by about five points. She faces state Rep. Derek Merrin, who has raised over $1.5 million, and a Libertarian candidate. Kaptur holds a decisive financial edge, with $3.5 million on hand and no outside opposition spending so far.\n\nExpert ratings split between Lean D and Tossup, with one outlet calling it a Republican flip opportunity. Prediction markets lean Democratic, though PredictIt is more cautious. Public polling is sparse; the only recent survey, a DCCC internal, shows a 48-48 tie. Republican surrogates including Vance, Johnson, and Ramaswamy have campaigned heavily for Merrin, signaling national investment in the race. The forecast gives Kaptur a narrow edge with substantial uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7474, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7282, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7108, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6729, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6764, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7175, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7321, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7015, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7133, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7126, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6869, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.72, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6326, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6614, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 2.5}, {"date"